{
  "id": "Compound::DB00802 - Gene::1576",
  "verbalization": "Alfentanil, a full opioid agonist, is linked to Cyp3a4 through multiple pathways that collectively suggest a role in the metabolism of substrates involving the cytochrome P450 3A4 enzyme. Pathway 1 demonstrates a direct binding of Alfentanil to Orm1, which is then bound by Acenocoumarol, ultimately leading to Cyp3a4 binding. Pathway 2 reveals that Alfentanil is included in the class of full opioid agonists, which includes Sufentanil, a compound that directly binds to Cyp3a4. Pathway 3 highlights that Alfentanil causes dependence on opiates, which is then influenced by Naloxone, a compound that binds to Cyp3a4. These pathways collectively imply that Alfentanil may influence Cyp3a4 through indirect mechanisms involving opioid receptor activation or metabolic substrates. The integration of these evidence strands suggests that Alfentanil may modulate Cyp3a4 activity through a complex interplay of receptor activation and metabolic pathways, potentially affecting drug metabolism and pharmacological outcomes.",
